        <definition>Status api::v2::Http::statusForException</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::exception &amp;e)</argsstring>
        <name>statusForException</name>
        <qualifiedname>api::v2::Http::statusForException</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::exception &amp;</type>
          <declname>e</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Selects the HTTP status corresponding to a caught exception. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref> means no database connection was available, so the client is told 503 and may retry; all other failures are 500. Used by the CRITICALMESSAGERESPONSE macro. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">e</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The caught exception to classify. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><ref refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2_1_1Http_1a6199aeb84d745378b1befef28d78892faaa8f68ec2a12ee4e1b4766e3fe760220" kindref="member">Status::SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE</ref> for <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref>, otherwise <ref refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2_1_1Http_1a6199aeb84d745378b1befef28d78892fac8c2d75c3c4886183816956f75b32501" kindref="member">Status::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Classification uses dynamic_cast, so it relies on the exception being polymorphic (as all std::exception-derived types are). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
